<article class="env-lemma" id="060EE1">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/060EE1">Lemma <span data-tag="060EE1">5.5.5.13</span>.</a> Let </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [r]^{f} \ar [d]^{g} &amp;  X' \ar [d] \\ Y \ar [r]^{f'} &amp;  Y' } \]
</div>
  <p> be a pushout diagram in an $\infty $-category $\calC $. Then there exists an isomorphism </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \bHom _{\calC _{X/}}(f,g) \simeq \bHom _{\calC _{Y/}}(f', \id _{Y}) \]
</div>
  <p> in the homotopy category $\calH $. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      According to Corollary <a href="/tag/3E8A7D" data-tag="3E8A7D">4.2.4.7</a>, we can assume without loss of generality that $\calC $ is the nerve of a fibrant simplicial category $\calD $, and that the diagram in question is the nerve of a commutative diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { X \ar [r]^{f} \ar [d]^{g} &amp;  X' \ar [d] \\ Y \ar [r]^{f'} &amp;  Y' } \]
</div>
    <p>
       in $\calD $. Theorem <a href="/tag/EB2834" data-tag="EB2834">4.2.4.1</a> implies that this diagram is homotopy coCartesian in $\calD $, so that we have a homotopy pullback diagram 
    <p>
      <div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { \bHom _{\calD }(Y', Y) \ar [r]^{\phi } \ar [d] &amp;  \bHom _{\calD }(Y,Y) \ar [d] \\ \bHom _{\calD }(X',Y) \ar [r]^{\phi '} &amp;  \bHom _{\calD }(X,Y) } \]
</div>
    <p>
       of Kan complexes. Consequently, we obtain an isomorphism in $\calH $ between the homotopy fiber of $\phi $ over $\id _{Y}$ and the homotopy fiber of $\phi '$ over $g$. According to Lemma <a href="/tag/461171" data-tag="461171">5.5.5.12</a>, these homotopy fibers may be identified with $\bHom _{\calC _{Y/}}(f', \id _{Y})$ and $ \bHom _{\calC _{X/}}(f,g)$, respectively. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>